---
description: When to pass a turn through unmarked
---

Pass through: bare slash commands (`/help`, `/lfg`, `/ce-plan`), raw
paths, command-like shell lines (including destructive `rm -rf`),
sticky opt-out, and autonomy-grant-only turns. A slash command plus
an English job is a task, not pass-through.

Casual register is not a rewrite reason. `json` / `be concise` alone is
a channel annotation, not an uplift gap. When routing is uncertain, pass
through.

Quoted or interrogative “stop rewriting…” must not sticky-opt-out.
Unbound “continue” with nothing to bind must not invent a pending task.
